## Rules to Follow

- You must always commit your changes whenever you update code. 
- You must always try and write code that is well documented. (self or commented is fine)
- You must only work on a single feature at a time.
- You must explain your decisions thouroughly to the user.
- You must always create a feature branch before writing any code. After completing the work, provide merge instructions in a MERGE.md file that explains how to merge the changes back to main with both a GitHub PR route and a GitHub CLI route.